/-!
# Local Held quotient geometry

The checked reductions transport local quotient calculations through actual
local conjugation and obtain normalizer containment from a four-point orbit
in a six-point action. The literal local subgroups have proved surjective
actions on six letters, factored through M/O₂(M). For all four published
representatives, the local two-core commutator equals that core and the
residual two-core image has a four-point orbit whose full stabilizer preimage
is the pair-product image. The source adapter combines these calculations
with exhaustive simultaneous local conjugacy.

Sources: GLS3 Table 5.3p; ATLAS max3/max4; Aschbacher–Smith, printed
pp.509–511 and 747–748.
-/
